is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0, leaf_router_0_1, spine_router_0_0, spine_router_0_1, super_spine_router_0
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the FRRouting control-plane daemons (bgpd/zebra) across the whole fabric, not a single “switch.” Mechanism: when bgpd/zebra restart, all BGP adjacencies reset. During the 1–2 minutes it takes for sessions to re-establish and routes to propagate, inter-VLAN traffic (pc_0_0 ↔ pc_0_1) briefly blackholes, then recovers—appearing as connectivity “up and down.”

Localization and evidence: On every router, bgpd and zebra PIDs show very recent start times (~130 seconds elapsed when checked). frr.log on all routers contains “Configuration Read in Took…” at 14:45:09 UTC, and “show bgp summary” on all nodes reports peer Up/Do
[FINAL] stop=no-more-tool-calls tool_calls=55
[SUBMITTED] parsed_ok=True is_anomaly=True faulty_devices=['leaf_router_0_0', 'leaf_router_0_1', 'spine_router_0_0', 'spine_router_0_1', 'super_spine_router_0']
[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_0, leaf_router_0_1, spine_router_0_0, spine_router_0_1, super_spine_router_0
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the FRRouting control-plane daemons (bgpd/zebra) across the whole fabric, not a single “switch.” Mechanism: when bgpd/zebra restart, all BGP adjacencies reset. During the 1–2 minutes it takes for sessions to re-establish and routes to propagate, inter-VLAN traffic (pc_0_0 ↔ pc_0_1) briefly blackholes, then recovers—appearing as connectivity “up and down.”

Localization and evidence: On every router, bgpd and zebra PIDs show very recent start times (~130 seconds elapsed when checked). frr.log on all routers contains “Configuration Read in Took…” at 14:45:09 UTC, and “show bgp summary” on all nodes reports peer Up/Down ≈ 00:01:52, proving a simultaneous restart of FRR daemons fabric-wide around 14:45. This is not an interface/link issue (all links show LOWER_UP, zero errors) and not isolated to leaf_router_0_0.

Root cause: FRR was restarted across all routers around 14:45 UTC (likely by an external supervisor or automation invoking frrinit.sh/watchfrr), resetting all BGP sessions simultaneously.

Corrective fix: Stop the external/duplicate FRR control and run FRR under a single manager. Specifically: enable/start the systemd frr.service on each router (and ensure only systemd controls watchfrr/bgpd/zebra), remove any out‑of‑band restart scripts, and disable periodic restarts. As a resilience enhancement, enable BGP graceful-restart on all peers so brief control-plane bounces don’t drop traffic. With restarts eliminated, the PCs’ connectivity will remain stable (pings are clean now). 
=== END ===